n injected `finalize`, and an in-memory config reader. Doctor probes take an","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./scripts/redact.jq","matches":[{"lineNumber":8,"content":"  # claude: init lists the user's MCP servers, plugins, skills, commands, memory paths","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":10,"content":"      with_entries(if .key | IN(\"mcp_servers\", \"slash_commands\", \"skills\", \"plugins\", \"agents\", \"memory_paths\", \"messaging_socket_path\")","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-18-nonblocking-wait.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":88,"content":"- The job registry currently tracks all job state purely in memory, with no persisted record","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-18-nonblocking-wait.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":62,"content":"    existing reference to the short name (forge's `dispatch.md`, skills, memory). Task 5 notes","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":68,"content":"- `src/job-registry.ts`'s `Job` type and `makeJobRegistry` closure hold all state in-memory","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":666,"content":"Updating the old short-name references (forge's `dispatch.md`, skills, memory) is the separate,","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":682,"content":"working CLI is `~/.local/bin/claude`, on PATH only interactively (matches prior memory); used its","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./docs/ideas/multi-backend.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":10,"content":"One server instead of four also saves memory: each stdio MCP server is a","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./CODE-REVIEW.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":99,"content":"On the finalize hot path (every completed write job) it spawns `rev-parse`, then `rev-list`, `diff --name-only`, `diff --stat`, `status --porcelain` strictly one at a time. The four post-`rev-parse` calls are independent → `Promise.all` cuts latency from ~5× to ~2× spawn round-trips. Separately, lines 60-62 duplicate `captureHead`'s exact `rev-parse HEAD → trim || null` logic.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":82,"totalMatchedLines":82,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_8340b766-b2b8-4c1c-a324-31a2caaa110","startedAtMs":"1790845459970","completedAtMs":"1790845460539"},"model_call_id":"a380c011-da4d-41b0-b1f6-64024bf8ce86-1-4owb","session_id":"d0cbbbf5-5deb-40e3-a6cf-fb1778573e0a","timestamp_ms":1790845460540}
