tions**\\n- #7/#4 detached supervisor + file-only truth vs `job_registry` in-process threads and RAM state — **Ruling:** real supervisor; files are SoT.\\n- #4 `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` vs `status_record.rs` `cursor-delegate-jobs` — **Ruling:** `delegate-jobs` per #4.\\n- #4 RUNNING record needs supervisor pid; `PollResult::Running` has none — **Ruling:** add `supervisorPid`.\\n- #4 cwd lock file across processes vs in-memory `path_lock` — **Ruling:** file lock for CLI BUSY.\\n- #4 terminal record must carry resume fields (cwd, capability, gate); `RunOutput` lacks them — **Ruling:** `resume` object on disk.\\n- #7 STATUS-only prompt vs `compose_prompt` preamble/verify on MCP path — **Ruling:** CLI STATUS-only; MCP unchanged.\\n- #7 tracer omits `--gate`/`--tool-idle-ms` that #4 documents — **Ruling:** defer flags; core path first.\\n\\n**2. Unstated defaults**\\n- Job id: `random_uuid()` — **Ruling:* [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":316,"content":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"duration_ms\":41566,\"duration_api_ms\":41566,\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Gathering issues #7 and #4 and reading the referenced source files.\\n\\n\\nFetching issue #4 body and checking for CLI/supervisor patterns.\\n\\n\\n**1. Contradictions**\\n- #7/#4 detached supervisor + file-only truth vs `job_registry` in-process threads and RAM state — **Ruling:** real supervisor; files are SoT.\\n- #4 `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` vs `status_record.rs` `cursor-delegate-jobs` — **Ruling:** `delegate-jobs` per #4.\\n- #4 RUNNING record needs supervisor pid; `PollResult::Running` has none — **Ruling:** add `supervisorPid`.\\n- #4 cwd lock file across processes vs in-memory `path_lock` — **Ruling:** file lock for CLI BUSY.\\n- #4 terminal record must carry resume fields (cwd, capability, gate); `RunOutput` lacks them — **Ruling:** `resume` object on disk.\\n- #7 STATUS-only prompt vs `compose_prompt` preamble/verify on MCP path — **Ruling:** CLI STATUS-only; MCP unchanged.\\n- #7 t [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"tests/fixtures/cursor/ponytail-18.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":44,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"completed\",\"call_id\":\"tool_531743bc-380b-4559-bf74-50d56b892ec\",\"tool_call\":{\"readToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"path\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-6-record-fixtures/scripts/redact.jq\"},\"result\":{\"success\":{\"content\":\"# Strip the recording user's personal setup from a headless stream line; keep the shape parsers see.\\ndef blank: if type == \\\"array\\\" then [] elif type == \\\"object\\\" then {} else \\\"\\\" end;\\ndef redact: walk(\\n  if type != \\\"object\\\" then . else\\n  # pi: system prompt sections (skills, context files, extension prompts) and extension tools (names kept)\\n    (if (.sections | type) == \\\"object\\\" then .sections |= map_values(\\\"[redacted]\\\") else . end)\\n  | (if (.toolsAdded | type) == \\\"array\\\" then .toolsAdded |= map({name}) else . end)\\n  # claude: init lists the user's MCP servers, plugins, skills, commands, memory paths\\n  | (if .type == \\\"system\\\" and .subtype == \\\"init\\\" then\\n      with_entries(if .key | IN(\\\"mcp_servers\\\", \\\"slash_commands\\\", \\\"skills [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":105,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"completed\",\"call_id\":\"tool_7c7c53bc-c228-417b-9c3a-249362c25ab\",\"tool_call\":{\"readToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"path\":\"/Users/user/.cursor/projects/Users-user-work-delegate-6-record-fixtures/agent-tools/119c6ec8-e9e6-42c3-adef-5753f728adc1.txt\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":90},\"result\":{\"success\":{\"content\":\"diff --git a/scripts/record.sh b/scripts/record.sh\\nnew file mode 100755\\nindex 0000000..d5488c9\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/scripts/record.sh\\n@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@\\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n+# Run one prompt through a backend's raw headless CLI and save stdout/stderr as a parser fixture.\\n+#\\n+#   scripts/record.sh BACKEND MODEL CAPABILITY NAME [CWD] [SESSION] < prompt\\n+#\\n+# BACKEND: cursor | pi | claude. CAPABILITY: read-only | read-write (pi rejects read-only).\\n+# SESSION resumes that backend session; pi and claude get a fresh id when it is omitted.\\n+# CANCEL_AFTER=N sends the CLI SIGTERM after N seconds.\\n+# Writes tests/fixtures/BACKEND/NAME.{stdout,stderr,argv}; prints the  [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"tests/fixtures/cursor/lane-8-ci.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":22,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"completed\",\"call_id\":\"tool_d453d59d-0908-4eaf-a7ea-bbc839b4071\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-8-ci && gh issue view 8 && gh issue view 4\",\"workingDirectory\":\"\",\"timeout\":30000,\"toolCallId\":\"tool_d453d59d-0908-4eaf-a7ea-bbc839b4071\",\"simpleCommands\":[\"cd\",\"gh\",\"gh\"],\"hasInputRedirect\":false,\"hasOutputRedirect\":false,\"parsingResult\":{\"parsingFailed\":false,\"executableCommands\":[{\"name\":\"cd\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-8-ci\"}],\"fullText\":\"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-8-ci\"},{\"name\":\"gh\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"issue\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\":\"8\"}],\"fullText\":\"gh issue view 8\"},{\"name\":\"gh\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"issue\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\":\"4\"}],\"fullText\":\"gh issue view 4\"}],\"hasRedirects\":false,\"hasCommandSubstitution\":false,\"redirects\":[]},\"fileOutputThresholdBytes\":\"40000\",\"isBackground\":false,\" [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"tests/fixtures/claude/review-19.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":9,"content":"{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"commands_changed\",\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"autonomous-flywheel\",\"description\":\"Flywheel unattended multi-PR landing: implement, triage CI, merge on green, morning report. Fires when asked to land a stack of PRs unattended or continue a flywheel session. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"clear-communication\",\"description\":\"Write and edit prose in GOV.UK / GDS style — plain English, active voice, front-loaded, sentence case, no bold/italic emphasis. Use when writing or editing reports, research write-ups, guidance, documentation, summaries, or any prose where clarity and accessibility matter. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"code-review\",\"description\":\"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":10,"content":"{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"init\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-8-ci\",\"session_id\":\"26c5e6c8-864e-4d87-8aa1-c1ca5a12b9c9\",\"tools\":[\"Task\",\"Bash\",\"CronCreate\",\"CronDelete\",\"CronList\",\"DesignSync\",\"Edit\",\"EnterWorktree\",\"ExitWorktree\",\"ListAgents\",\"Monitor\",\"NotebookEdit\",\"PushNotification\",\"Read\",\"RemoteTrigger\",\"ReportFindings\",\"ScheduleWakeup\",\"SendMessage\",\"Skill\",\"TaskStop\",\"ToolSearch\",\"WebFetch\",\"WebSearch\",\"Workflow\",\"Write\"],\"mcp_servers\":[],\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"permissionMode\":\"plan\",\"slash_commands\":[],\"terminal_slash_commands\":[\"doctor\",\"color\",\"focus\",\"reload-plugins\"],\"apiKeySource\":\"none\",\"claude_code_version\":\"2.1.286\",\"output_style\":\"no-slop\",\"agents\":[],\"skills\":[],\"plugins\":[],\"capabilities\":[\"interrupt_receipt_v1\",\"interrupt_cancel_queued_v1\",\"msg_lifecycle_v1\",\"sdk_mcp_tools_list_changed\",\"sdk_mcp_manifests\",\"mcp_read_resource_v1\",\"mcp_tool_ui_meta_v1\"],\"analytics_disabled\":false,\"product_feedback_disabled\":false,\"uuid\":\"45546231-f45f-4dcc-a0b6-f43c1f17ef4 [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":16,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01CtvwRn678gy36PGvnifeBK\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\tci: Linux workflow (fmt, clippy, tests) (#8)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t19\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/19\\nadditions:\\t23\\ndeletions:\\t0\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #8\\n\\nOne `ci` job on `ubuntu-latest` for pull requests and pushes to `main`: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`. Ignored live tests stay excluded. Every action is pinned by SHA, the token is read-only, and `pull_request_target` is not used.\\n\\nImplemented by composer-2.5 via `scripts/record.sh` (fixture lands with #18).\\n\\nCo-authored with Claude Code.\\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..ede11d5\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @ [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":31,"content":"{\"duration_api_ms\":18398,\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"26c5e6c8-864e-4d87-8aa1-c1ca5a12b9c9\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.14755359999999998,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":8,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":27102,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":110698,\"output_tokens\":1699,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":359},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2