{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_59329880-b12b-4f53-836a-3df6e5c59c5","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 9 --json body,title 2>/dev/null | head -5; gh issue view 10 --json body 2>/dev/null | head -3","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_59329880-b12b-4f53-836a-3df6e5c59c5","simpleCommands":["cd","gh","head","gh","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"9"},{"type":"word","value":"--json"},{"type":"word","value":"body,title"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 9 --json body,title"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-5"}],"fullText":"head -5"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"10"},{"type":"word","value":"--json"},{"type":"word","value":"body"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 10 --json body"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-3"}],"fullText":"head -3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Quick peek at issues 9-10 scope","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"d0cbbbf5-5deb-40e3-a6cf-fb1778573e0a","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"a380c011-da4d-41b0-b1f6-64024bf8ce86"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 9 --json body,title 2>/dev/null | head -5; gh issue view 10 --json body 2>/dev/null | head -3","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"{\"body\":\"## Parent\\n\\n#4\\n\\n## What to build\\n\\nGround-truth verification and safety in the supervisor.\\n\\n- `--gate CMD` on `run`: the supervisor runs the gate after the agent; a failing gate downgrades DONE to DONE_WITH_CONCERNS and records the gate's output.\\n- The git change-set computed by the tool, and the concern when commits landed but the tree is still dirty.\\n- `--tool-idle-ms N`: the idle watchdog kills a job that goes silent past the model-idle or tool-idle window (defaults from the host profile) and reports it.\\n- A lock file per resolved `cwd`, held by a read-write job's supervisor. A second read-write job in the same `cwd` returns BUSY with the holder's job id, including from another process. Read-only jobs take no lock.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Gate pass and gate fail are reflected in the terminal record.\\n- [ ] The change-set lists what the agent changed and committed.\\n- [ ] A silent fake agent is killed after the window and the record says why.\\n- [ ] Two `delegate run` processes writing the same `cwd`: the second gets BUSY; the lock is released when the first finishes or dies.\\n- [ ] End-to-end tests cover each case.\\n\\n## Blocked by\\n\\n- #7 Tracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\",\"title\":\"Gate, change-set, watchdog and cross-process write lock\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Parent\\n\\n#4\\n\\n## What to build\\n\\n- `delegate resume <jobId> [--model M] [--capability C] [--gate CMD]`, prompt on stdin or `--prompt-file`. Reads the job's status record, reuses its model, cwd, capability, gate and tool-idle window, applies overrides, and starts a new job continuing the backend session. Works on any terminal status. A model override on a different backend is rejected. Returns a new job id.\\n- `delegate cancel <jobId>`: reads the supervisor pid from the record, signals its process group, and the record ends CANCELLED.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Resume continues the session (the fake agent sees the resume flag and session id) with the original settings.\\n- [ ] Each override replaces its stored value; a cross-backend model is rejected.\\n- [ ] Resume works when the original `run` and supervisor processes are gone.\\n- [ ] Cancel stops the agent and every process it started; the record says CANCELLED.\\n- [ ] End-to-end tests cover each case.\\n\\n## Blocked by\\n\\n- #7 Tracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\"}\n","stderr":"","executionTime":2212,"interleavedOutput":"{\"body\":\"## Parent\\n\\n#4\\n\\n## What to build\\n\\nGround-truth verification and safety in the supervisor.\\n\\n- `--gate CMD` on `run`: the supervisor runs the gate after the agent; a failing gate downgrades DONE to DONE_WITH_CONCERNS and records the gate's output.\\n- The git change-set computed by the tool, and the concern when commits landed but the tree is still dirty.\\n- `--tool-idle-ms N`: the idle watchdog kills a job that goes silent past the model-idle or tool-idle window (defaults from the host profile) and reports it.\\n- A lock file per resolved `cwd`, held by a read-write job's supervisor. A second read-write job in the same `cwd` returns BUSY with the holder's job id, including from another process. Read-only jobs take no lock.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Gate pass and gate fail are reflected in the terminal record.\\n- [ ] The change-set lists what the agent changed and committed.\\n- [ ] A silent fake agent is killed after the window and the record says why.\\n- [ ] Two `delegate run` processes writing the same `cwd`: the second gets BUSY; the lock is released when the first finishes or dies.\\n- [ ] End-to-end tests cover each case.\\n\\n## Blocked by\\n\\n- #7 Tracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\",\"title\":\"Gate, change-set, watchdog and cross-process write lock\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Parent\\n\\n#4\\n\\n## What to build\\n\\n- `delegate resume <jobId> [--model M] [--capability C] [--gate CMD]`, prompt on stdin or `--prompt-file`. Reads the job's status record, reuses its model, cwd, capability, gate and tool-idle window, applies overrides, and starts a new job continuing the backend session. Works on any terminal status. A model override on a different backend is rejected. Returns a new job id.\\n- `delegate cancel <jobId>`: reads the supervisor pid from the record, signals its process group, and the record ends CANCELLED.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Resume continues the session (the fake agent sees the resume flag and session id) with the original settings.\\n- [ ] Each override replaces its stored value; a cross-backend model is rejected.\\n- [ ] Resume works when the original `run` and supervisor processes are gone.\\n- [ ] Cancel stops the agent and every process it started; the record says CANCELLED.\\n- [ ] End-to-end tests cover each case.\\n\\n## Blocked by\\n\\n- #7 Tracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\"}\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1906},"isBackground":false},"description":"Quick peek at issues 9-10 scope"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_59329880-b12b-4f53-836a-3df6e5c59c5","startedAtMs":"1790845474296","completedAtMs":"1790845476713"},"model_call_id":"a380c011-da4d-41b0-b1f6-64024bf8ce86-4-tmw4","session_id":"d0cbbbf5-5deb-40e3-a6cf-fb1778573e0a","timestamp_ms":1790845476693}
