{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### 1. Contradictions\n- **AC “sleep before printing the id”** vs fake `SLOW` (agent only): id return is gated on the RUNNING record, not agent speed → **`DELEGATE_RUN_DELAY_MS` before `println` in `run`.**\n- **Memory “supervisor”** vs timing the `delegate` parent: supervisor is `__supervise` → **sample RSS of `supervisorPid` from the record.**\n- **#12 lists resume/cancel/doctor/models** vs `origin/main` `cli.rs` (only `run`/`watch`): → **build on post–#9–#11 tree; not a doc bug given your assumption.**\n\n### 2. Unstated defaults\n- **Memory metric/API** → **Linux: max VmRSS from `/proc/<pid>/status` during RUNNING; budget 3× measured, same as latency.**\n- **Latency endpoint** → **wall clock: `run`/`resume` until id on stdout; others until process exit.**\n- **`watch` case** → **finished terminal job(s), no `--timeout` poll.**\n- **`cancel` budget** → **RUNNING job, SIGTERM path (not the 5s SIGKILL stall).**\n- **Recorded “measured”** → **constants in test with comment showing baseline and 3× cap.**\n\n### 3. Failure cases (no behaviour)\n- **CI timing flake** → **fail hard; no retries (margin is the fix).**\n- **RSS unreadable / pid gone** → **fail test after short wait for RUNNING + pid.**\n- **doctor hard-fail (exit 1)** → **still bound; use fakes that exit 0.**\n\n### 4. Acceptance criteria vs spec/code\n- **“Every command” + `watch --timeout`** fights #7 (exit 1 after wall time) → **budget only instant terminal `watch`; timeout stays separate e2e.**\n- **Negative slow-`run` without a CLI hook** can’t be implemented from fake agent alone → **require delay env + unit-style e2e that lowers budget.**\n- **Memory “Linux CI”** vs spec’s macOS-local suite → **`#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]` memory test or CI-only job; latency tests on all targets.**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS"}]},"session_id":"d0cbbbf5-5deb-40e3-a6cf-fb1778573e0a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":52248,"duration_api_ms":52248,"is_error":false,"result":"Gathering GitHub issues, rulings, and relevant code for the preflight.\n### 1. Contradictions\n- **AC “sleep before printing the id”** vs fake `SLOW` (agent only): id return is gated on the RUNNING record, not agent speed → **`DELEGATE_RUN_DELAY_MS` before `println` in `run`.**\n- **Memory “supervisor”** vs timing the `delegate` parent: supervisor is `__supervise` → **sample RSS of `supervisorPid` from the record.**\n- **#12 lists resume/cancel/doctor/models** vs `origin/main` `cli.rs` (only `run`/`watch`): → **build on post–#9–#11 tree; not a doc bug given your assumption.**\n\n### 2. Unstated defaults\n- **Memory metric/API** → **Linux: max VmRSS from `/proc/<pid>/status` during RUNNING; budget 3× measured, same as latency.**\n- **Latency endpoint** → **wall clock: `run`/`resume` until id on stdout; others until process exit.**\n- **`watch` case** → **finished terminal job(s), no `--timeout` poll.**\n- **`cancel` budget** → **RUNNING job, SIGTERM path (not the 5s SIGKILL stall).**\n- **Recorded “measured”** → **constants in test with comment showing baseline and 3× cap.**\n\n### 3. Failure cases (no behaviour)\n- **CI timing flake** → **fail hard; no retries (margin is the fix).**\n- **RSS unreadable / pid gone** → **fail test after short wait for RUNNING + pid.**\n- **doctor hard-fail (exit 1)** → **still bound; use fakes that exit 0.**\n\n### 4. Acceptance criteria vs spec/code\n- **“Every command” + `watch --timeout`** fights #7 (exit 1 after wall time) → **budget only instant terminal `watch`; timeout stays separate e2e.**\n- **Negative slow-`run` without a CLI hook** can’t be implemented from fake agent alone → **require delay env + unit-style e2e that lowers budget.**\n- **Memory “Linux CI”** vs spec’s macOS-local suite → **`#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]` memory test or CI-only job; latency tests on all targets.**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS","sessio